    ["Complete: 'Despite ___ for hours, they failed to reach an agreement.'", "negotiating", ["they negotiated", "to negotiate", "negotiate"], "Setelah 'despite' dipakai gerund, bukan klausa atau infinitif."],
    ["Which sentence is NOT acceptable?", "Even though costs increased, but productivity did not fall.", ["Even though costs increased, productivity did not fall.", "Costs increased, but productivity did not fall.", "Despite rising costs, productivity did not fall."], "Konsesi tidak boleh ditandai dua kali dengan 'even though' dan 'but'."],
    ["Complete: '___ classical theory predicts stability, empirical data suggest volatility.'", "Whereas", ["Despite", "However", "In spite of"], "'Whereas' menghubungkan dua klausa yang berlawanan dengan bobot setara."],
    ["Complete: 'The project was a success, ___ a costly one.'", "albeit", ["despite", "although it", "whereas"], "'Albeit' dapat langsung diikuti frasa benda untuk menambahkan konsesi."],
    ["Which sentence uses 'though' correctly at the end of a clause?", "The report was late. It was excellent, though.", ["Though the report was late. It was excellent.", "The report was late, though it excellent.", "The report was late; though, it excellent was."], "'Though' di akhir kalimat berfungsi seperti 'however' dan menyatakan kontras."],
    ["Combine formally within one clause: 'The improvement was real. It was small.'", "The improvement was real, albeit small.", ["The improvement was real, despite small.", "The improvement was real, although small it.", "The improvement was real, whereas small."], "'Albeit + adjektiva' menambahkan konsesi secara ringkas dan formal."],
    ["Complete: 'Much ___ I admire her work, I cannot support this proposal.'", "as", ["like", "even", "so"], "Ungkapan 'Much as + klausa' berarti 'walaupun sangat' dan bersifat konsesif."],
    ["Why is 'Although the data were limited, but the conclusion is valid' wrong?", "It marks concession twice, with 'although' and 'but'.", ["'Although' cannot be followed by a past tense verb.", "'Data' must always take a singular verb in English.", "'But' must always come at the start of a sentence."], "Bahasa Inggris tidak memakai 'although' dan 'but' bersamaan dalam satu kalimat."],
    ["Complete: '___ the high price, the tickets sold out within an hour.'", "In spite of", ["Even though", "Although", "Whereas"], "'The high price' adalah frasa benda, sehingga dipakai 'in spite of', bukan konjungsi."]
